  <!-- author -->


    <div class="container-full-width container--padding">
      <div class="container-md">
        <div class="editor-output leading-text editor-output--responsive-img">
          <p>Two big names were eliminated from the race for the EHF Champions League Men main round in round 5 on Thursday: Montpellier Handball following their 40:34 defeat at Barça, and OTP Bank - PICK Szeged after their 33:33 draw against GOG. The Danish side, meanwhile, became the ninth team to secure a main round berth. The remaining three qualification spots will be decided in the final round, including both places still up for grabs in Group B. Ahead of the decisive matches, MT Melsungen, Orlen Wisla Plock and HBC Nantes are all level on six points after MT's victory against the Polish side. In Group E, round 6 will also determine the second qualification spot behind Barça, with either SAH - Aarhus (five points) or Dinamo Bucuresti (three) progressing. While Barça and SC Magdeburg maintained their perfect records, Kolstad Håndball and IFK Kristianstad remain without a point ahead of their final matches.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

<script async type="text/plain" class="_iub_cs_activate js-consent-script" data-iub-purposes="3" data-suppressedsrc="https://platform.twitter.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
<script async type="text/plain" class="_iub_cs_activate js-consent-script" data-iub-purposes="3" data-suppressedsrc="https://www.instagram.com/embed.js" charset="utf-8"></script>



  <div class="container-full-width container--padding" >
    <div class="content-container container-sm">
      <div class="content-block">
        <div class="editor-output editor-output--responsive-img js-consent-content" data-purposes="3">
          <ul><li><p><strong>With three consecutive saves in crunch time, goalkeeper Nebojsa Simić proved to be MT Melsungen's X-factor in their 28:26 win against Orlen Wisla Plock.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Mario Šoštarić's nine goals were not enough for OTP Bank - PICK Szeged. The Hungarian side needed a victory to stay in the race for the main round, but ultimately had to settle for a 33:33 draw against GOG.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Barça's 9:3 run ended Montpellier Handball's hopes after a strong start, with three Barça players scoring seven goals each.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Francisco Costa set a new personal EHF Champions League scoring record with 14 goals in Sporting CP's 42:40 win against IFK Kristianstad.</strong></p></li><li><p><strong>Fourteen saves from Dominik Kuzmanović, 11 goals from Philipp Weber and a strong second-half display paved the way for SC Magdeburg's away win at Kolstad Håndball.</strong></p></li></ul><p></p>
        </div>


<div class="consent-info js-consent-info" data-purposes="3">
    <div class="consent-info-content">
        <h2>This content is blocked</h2>
        <p>You said no to using cookies or similar tools that help improve your experience. To see this content, you would need to update your <a href="javascript:void(0);" class="iubenda-cs-preferences-link">Privacy Preferences</a>.</p>
        <button class="iubenda-cs-preferences-link" data-accept-purposes="3">
            Update
        </button>
    </div>
</div>      </div>
    </div>
  </div>


  <div class="container-full-width container--padding" >
    <div class="content-container container-sm">
      <div class="content-block">
        <div class="editor-output editor-output--responsive-img js-consent-content" data-purposes="3">
          <p>GROUP B</p><h3><a data-router-slot="disabled" data-anchor="#http://ehfcl.eurohandball.com/men/2026-27/matches/details/202711020101019/MTMelsungen-OrlenWislaPlock/" href="#http://ehfcl.eurohandball.com/men/2026-27/matches/details/202711020101019/MTMelsungen-OrlenWislaPlock/" title="#http://ehfcl.eurohandball.com/men/2026-27/matches/details/202711020101019/MTMelsungen-OrlenWislaPlock/" type="external">MT Melsungen (GER) vs Orlen Wisla Plock (POL) 28:26 (15:14)</a></h3><p>H2H: 1-0-1<br>Top scorer: Eric Balenciaga 6/6, Aaron Mensing 6/11 (both MT Melsungen), Frederik Bjerre 4/7, Sergei Mark Kosorotov 4/6 (both Orlen Wisla Plock)</p><p>As expected, it turned into a close and hard-fought battle. From 8:7 in the 19th minute onwards, the hosts never trailed again, but Plock proved to be the tough opponent many had expected, relying on a physically strong defence and efficient wing play in attack. Melsungen’s biggest lead in the first half was two goals, and although they made the better start to the second half, Plock remained within touching distance, even after defensive specialist Leon Šušnja received a red card following his third suspension. But, just as in the previous home win against Nantes, goalkeeper Nebojsa Simić proved to be the decisive factor in crunch time, finishing with 11 saves. Three stops in a row helped MT open up a 26:23 lead, which they largely maintained until the final whistle. After losing the reverse fixture 25:24, the German side are now not only level on points with Plock (and Nantes) on six, but also hold the head-to-head advantage by a one-goal margin.</p><p><span class="umb-embed-holder" data-embed-constrain="true" data-embed-height="393" data-embed-url="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7S8V31BEaKk&amp;pp=ygUUZWhmIGhvbWUgb2YgaGFuZGJhbGw%3D" data-embed-width="700"><iframe width="699" height="393" class="_iub_cs_activate" data-iub-purposes="3" data-suppressedsrc="https://www.youtube.com/embed/7S8V31BEaKk?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen="" title="MT Melsungen vs Orlen Wisla Plock | Highlights | EHF Champions League Men 2026/27"></iframe></span></p>
        </div>


<div class="consent-info js-consent-info" data-purposes="3">
    <div class="consent-info-content">
        <h2>This content is blocked</h2>
        <p>You said no to using cookies or similar tools that help improve your experience. To see this content, you would need to update your <a href="javascript:void(0);" class="iubenda-cs-preferences-link">Privacy Preferences</a>.</p>
        <button class="iubenda-cs-preferences-link" data-accept-purposes="3">
            Update
        </button>
    </div>
</div>      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

<div class="container-full-width container--padding">
    <div class="container">
