  <div class="container-full-width container--padding" >
    <div class="content-container container-sm">
      <div class="content-block">
        <div class="editor-output editor-output--responsive-img js-consent-content" data-purposes="3">
          <p>GROUP E</p><h3><a data-router-slot="disabled" href="https://ehfcl.eurohandball.com/men/2026-27/matches/details/202711020101049/Bar%C3%A7a-MontpellierHandball/" title="ehfcl.eurohandball.com" type="external">Barça (ESP) vs Montpellier Handball (FRA) 40:34 (20:18)</a></h3><p>H2H: 11-1-4<br>Top scorer: Timothy N’Guessan 7/11, Luis Frade 7/7, Aleix Gómez 7/8 (all Barça); Kylian Villeminot 6/11, Agustin Casado 6/10 (both Montpellier Handball)</p><p>After losing three matches in a row, Montpellier Handball had their backs against the wall, as even a draw against the defending and record champions would not have been enough to keep their hopes of a main round spot alive. The side coached by Érick Mathé were eager to pull off a miracle at the famous Palau Blaugrana, but they could only do so for the opening 24 minutes. At that point, Montpellier led 18:16, but then conceded a 4:0 Barça run before the break and found themselves trailing 25:21 in the 35th minute. While their attack flowed well, the French side lacked the necessary defensive stability and allowed Barça too many easy goals from all areas of the court. After Blaz Janc scored for the hosts' first five-goal lead of the night at 30:25 in the 43rd minute, Benjamin Richert received a direct red card for pushing Daniel Fernández, dealing another blow to Montpellier. By the time French superstar Dika Mem made it 34:28 in a one-sided second half, Montpellier’s fate was sealed.</p>
        </div>


<div class="consent-info js-consent-info" data-purposes="3">
    <div class="consent-info-content">
